  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Candyman - No Lead Vocals, Full Ending** (1 review): Very faint traces of vocals can be heard on Candyman if you listen closely [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Playin' In The Band #1**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n- **Playin' In The Band #2**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [7]\n- **Playin' In The Band #3**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bird Song #1**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bird Song #2**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bird Song #3**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bird Song #4**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Bird Song #5**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **gd1971-02-01.sbd.Studio.Rehearsal.120486.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 13 songs; 48 min; rated 1.6/5 by 5 [1]. Said about its sound: Sound quality is good, and the material is plain runthroughs without any jams [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Rehearsal run-through of newer songs in February 1971, ahead of the Capitol Theater shows [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **gd1971-02-01.sbd.Studio.Rehearsal.120486.flac16**: taped by Michael Lestatkatt; transferred by Michael Lestatkatt; source: unknown low gen Maxell XLII Cassette>Wav via Teac Stand Alone CD Burner > ? > SBE found - fix (TLH) shift backwards > MD5 + FFP made with (TLH) [1]. Also: June 2012 update: a rar file was sent to Norm, thanks to LESTATKATT; a shorten-file error was found and fixed; After the fix, the files were shifted backwards and the MD5 and FFP checksums were regenerated using TLH [1]",
